---
import ProjectArticle from '@components/gta6-leonida-atlas/ProjectArticle.astro';
import { urls } from '@lib/urls';
---

<ProjectArticle
  path={urls.leonidaAtlasCredits()}
  title="Credits & sources"
  section="Attribution"
  description="The atlas combines clearly attributed community cartography with references to official GTA 6 material."
>
  <section>
    <h2>GTADB community data</h2>
    <p>
      GTA VI Landmarks Data and GTA VI Map Tiles (CC BY 4.0) — <a href="https://map.gtadb.org"
        >GTADB / Map GTA</a
      >. Community map artwork: Yanis v16, distributed through GTADB.
    </p>
    <p>
      Generalized base geography is derived from the GTADB Yanis v16 raster tiles, pinned to commit
      <code>7c3f8c2</code>. Point evidence uses the landmark dataset from the same pinned source:
      2,198 records, including 2,091 positioned records and 107 records without coordinates.
    </p>
    <p>
      Source: <a
        href="https://github.com/rolux/gtadb.org/tree/7c3f8c295d64254e6b6d269b77c6f84fc4339f9c/maps"
        rel="noopener noreferrer">GTADB map data at the pinned commit</a
      >. These source-derived cartographic layers are used under
      <a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/" rel="license noopener noreferrer"
        >Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International</a
      >.
    </p>
    <p>
      Our presentation recolors and generalizes the source pixels, excludes non-geographic legend
      and screenshot areas, and adds decorative coast emphasis. The water halo is not bathymetry.
      Read the <a href="/assets/gta6-leonida-atlas/ATTRIBUTION.md">complete attribution</a> and <a
        href="/assets/gta6-leonida-atlas/metadata.json">generation manifest</a
      >.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section>
    <h2>Rockstar Games references</h2>
    <p>
      Official Rockstar Games trailers, screenshots and webpages inform appearance and evidence.
      Media shown in an evidence panel retains its cited source and separate rights status; it is
      not licensed with the project code or cartographic layer. Grand Theft Auto, GTA, Rockstar
      Games, their marks and official media belong to their respective rights holders. This
      independent project is not affiliated with, endorsed by or sponsored by Rockstar Games or
      Take-Two Interactive.
    </p>
    <p>
      <a href="https://www.rockstargames.com/VI" rel="noopener noreferrer"
        >Official Grand Theft Auto VI website</a
      >
    </p>
  </section>
  <section>
    <h2>Visual direction</h2>
    <p>
      A user-provided illustrated map informed the hierarchy, restrained linework and broad color
      language only. Its coastline, labels and geometry were not reused.
    </p>
    <p>
      Procedural geometry and generated material or vegetation studies are reconstruction assets,
      not extracted GTA VI game assets. Their reuse status remains separate from the CC BY 4.0 map
      data and is part of the source-release preparation.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section>
    <h2>Built with</h2>
    <p>
      Astro provides the project website, Three.js the 3D renderer, and native SVG the interactive
      coordinate layer. Inter and Oswald provide the interface typography. These dependencies retain
      their own licenses; they do not determine the license of this project's code.
    </p>
  </section>
</ProjectArticle>
